{
  "schema": "stdo.context-generation.constraint-map/1",
  "scenario": "S1",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "S1-01",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "The fictional owner asks for a repair candidate for /fictional/seed-context/candidate/context_select.py in source cut seed-r7. The method selected by its Product is the released basis in BASIS.json; this is an implementation repair with unchanged requirement and accepted design.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S1.md@sha256:acd89137b657a7d0025ae98133721fcd3f3f91dd3c4aa99e0d133a9a38a774a4#S1-01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S1-02",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "The function is select_context(records, roots, budget). The admitted domain is a finite list of uniquely identified records, a list of root IDs and a nonnegative integer budget. Records have a nonempty string id and a requires list of IDs; other JSON-compatible fields are opaque payload. Malformed types and duplicate record IDs are outside this task.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S1.md@sha256:acd89137b657a7d0025ae98133721fcd3f3f91dd3c4aa99e0d133a9a38a774a4#S1-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S1-03",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "The current helper computes reachable records but drops records whose standing is unresolved, then slices the result to budget and reports complete. The owner supplied this diagnosis as a starting observation, not an observed repair or passing test.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S1.md@sha256:acd89137b657a7d0025ae98133721fcd3f3f91dd3c4aa99e0d133a9a38a774a4#S1-03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S1-04",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "The requirement is the complete finite transitive dependency closure of the roots, with each whole record retained once and results sorted by id. A required record remains required regardless of its standing value. Inputs must remain unchanged.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S1.md@sha256:acd89137b657a7d0025ae98133721fcd3f3f91dd3c4aa99e0d133a9a38a774a4#S1-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S1-05",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "Success has exactly {status: complete, records: [...]}. If the full distinct closure exceeds budget, the result is exactly {status: refused, reason: budget_exceeded, records: []}. No partial successful result meets the requirement.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S1.md@sha256:acd89137b657a7d0025ae98133721fcd3f3f91dd3c4aa99e0d133a9a38a774a4#S1-05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S1-06",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "Unknown roots and dangling dependencies are explicit refusals with reasons unknown_root and dangling_reference. Dangling validation covers the entire supplied graph, including unselected records. Refusal precedence is unknown_root, then dangling_reference, then budget_exceeded.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S1.md@sha256:acd89137b657a7d0025ae98133721fcd3f3f91dd3c4aa99e0d133a9a38a774a4#S1-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S1-07",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "Valid cycles and duplicate paths are allowed. Empty roots with budget zero yield complete with an empty list when the entire graph is valid. The illustrative graph A requires B and C, with C unresolved, needs all three records and a budget of at least three.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S1.md@sha256:acd89137b657a7d0025ae98133721fcd3f3f91dd3c4aa99e0d133a9a38a774a4#S1-07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S1-08",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "Accepted design D-seed-2 uses a finite visited set and a work queue, then materializes complete records. It does not change the source record meanings or make an assessment decision. No requirement or design repricing is requested.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S1.md@sha256:acd89137b657a7d0025ae98133721fcd3f3f91dd3c4aa99e0d133a9a38a774a4#S1-08"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S1-09",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "The retained smoke result covers only one resolved root with no dependencies at seed-r7. It supplies no observation of the failing unresolved-dependency or budget cases; no successor candidate or independent review exists.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S1.md@sha256:acd89137b657a7d0025ae98133721fcd3f3f91dd3c4aa99e0d133a9a38a774a4#S1-09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S1-10",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "The fictional owner grant permits a separately bound Writer to read this brief, /fictional/seed-context/specification/requirements.md, /fictional/seed-context/design/D-seed-2.md, and the two candidate files, and edit only candidate/context_select.py and candidate/test_context_select.py. Focused in-memory Python checks and writing the run result to /fictional/seed-context/work/run-8/RETURN.md are permitted. No other project, Git, network, installation or publication operation is granted.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S1.md@sha256:acd89137b657a7d0025ae98133721fcd3f3f91dd3c4aa99e0d133a9a38a774a4#S1-10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S1-11",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "The accepted project frame permits one direct Writer for this pure local repair; it imposes no independent-review condition or durable ticket for a run-local result. The owner nevertheless requests proposed Executive, Worker and Reviewer context documents for inspection in this exercise. They are not instructions to activate every proposed role.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S1.md@sha256:acd89137b657a7d0025ae98133721fcd3f3f91dd3c4aa99e0d133a9a38a774a4#S1-11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S1-12",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "The target return is the exact repair candidate identity, changed paths, observed checks and remaining uncertainty, to the owner through run-8/RETURN.md. This scope ends within that run. There are no external effects to reconcile and no request to release or adopt a product.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S1.md@sha256:acd89137b657a7d0025ae98133721fcd3f3f91dd3c4aa99e0d133a9a38a774a4#S1-12"
      ]
    },
